12-Month High Performance Coaching Program Overview

This general coaching overview outlines a framework designed to help professionals shift from reactive overwork to calm, intentional effectiveness.
It will be tailored to individual needs after assessment.

Program Goals

 * Establish inner stability to distinguish core priorities from background noise.

 * Cultivate presence and adaptability to handle current challenges without bringing in past baggage.

 * Apply the Pareto Principle (80/20 Rule) to identify the 20% of effort that drives 80% of key outcomes, freeing up time to recharge, learn, or be with family.

 * Prevent burnout and mental/emotional overload by eliminating systematic overtime.

 * Achieve self-sufficiency and independence from coaching by the end of 12 months.

Program Structure & Logistics

 * Duration: 12 Months.

 * Monthly Cadence: 
One 60-minute thematic coaching session plus one 30-minute practical application/training session.
 
* Between-Session Support(billed extra): Asynchronous messaging (e.g., WhatsApp) for continuous feedback, accountability, and habit integration.

 * Format & Location: Hybrid delivery available—online or in-person sessions tailored to scheduling preferences.

 * Investment: 
€4,700 total (suggested schedule: two installments of €2,350, with a 6-month progress review).
Whatsapp support (not on Friday through Saturday) 280 € per month

Core Methodology & Focus Areas

 * Stress Response Control: Decoupling mental triggers from physiological stress responses to prevent hormone spikes.

 * Cognitive Pattern Breaking: Identifying and dismantling unproductive looping thoughts and procrastination drivers.

 * Emotional Processing: Uncovering trigger roots to manage and process emotions effectively under pressure.

 * Customized Learning: Tailored supplementary reading and exercises aligned with individual learning styles.


Preparatory Phase

Before starting, clients complete two foundational assessments to map baseline strengths and growth areas:

 * Adaptability Assessment

 * Five-Mountain Assessment: Evaluates physical, mental, emotional, intuition, and integrated action (Kokoro) dimensions.